edits. Nonzero local/ancestral priors are separately enumerated in standingPriors. Low/high standing-prior scales .3/2.8 are sensitivity choices. Parent stocks are debited for every departure. The declared common rate is calibrated against every low/central/high scenario at both1000 and5000 people per dot across all eight nonadditive geography variants, with a small funding buffer. It is not a historical fertility estimate.","sources":[{"id":"CLV2025","title":"Lazaridis et al. (2025), The genetic origin of the Indo-Europeans","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-024-08531-5","basis":"Broad source interpretation; no census calibration."},{"id":"TARIM2021","title":"Zhang et al. (2021), The genomic origins of the Bronze Age Tarim Basin mummies","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-021-04052-7","basis":"Broad source interpretation; no census calibration."},{"id":"CELTIC2026","title":"McColl et al. (2026), Celtic-associated dispersal","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-11198-9","basis":"Broad source interpretation; no census calibration."},{"id":"GERMANIC2026","title":"McColl et al. (2026), Germanic-associated dispersal","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09064-1","basis":"Broad source interpretation; no census calibration."},{"id":"SLAVIC2025","title":"Gretzinger et al. (2025), Ancient DNA connects large-scale migration with the spread of Slavs","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-025-09437-6","basis":"Broad source interpretation; no census calibration."},{"id":"BALKANS2023","title":"Olalde et al. (2023), Balkan genetic history","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2023.10.018","basis":"Broad source interpretation; no census calibration."}],"landscapes":{"CLV":{"points":[[47.383106,45.956232],[45.813721,48.116595],[46.686963,47.829053],[41.725835,47.421237],[45.713597,47.190776],[48.19861,46.880711],[44.36988,48.429837],[46.021098,47.482298],[45.292101,48.570869],[41.07084,49.516316],[48.05793,46.083396],[46.548331,47.4